{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses.</b> Since women are talkative, she pursued the matter more than Aaron; therefore Scripture placed her first, and she was punished more." "<b>Because a Cushite woman he had taken.</b> In the words of the chronicles of Moses it implies she was actually a Cushite — that she was a queen, and Moses ruled over Cush for forty years. And therefore they said: ״אך במשה דבר ה׳״ — that is, is it because the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke with him that he grew proud and did not wish to take a wife from the daughters of Israel? Did He not also speak with us, and we did not grow proud on that account? And it appears that they said this about that queen whom he had taken, for from Zipporah he fled because of Pharaoh, and was forced."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:15.655517877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}